{"cuisine/angolan-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/angolan-cuisine","n":"Angolan cuisine","c":"#e46a3f","crumb":[["Africa","cuisines#africa"],["Cuisine"]],"sub":"National cuisine of Angola","intro":[["Angolan cuisine consists of several dishes popular among nationals and foreigners, a fusion of indigenous African and Portuguese influences. These may include funge, mufete (grilled fish, plantain, sweet potato, cassava, and gari), calulu, moamba de galinha, moamba de ginguba, kissaca, and mukua sorbet."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"angolan-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Angolan_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[]}],"cont":"African cuisine","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/d/d3/Moambe_-_noix_de_palme_sauce_with_chicken.jpg/500px-Moambe_-_noix_de_palme_sauce_with_chicken.jpg","w":500,"h":398,"by":"T.K. Naliaka","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Moambe_-_noix_de_palme_sauce_with_chicken.jpg"}},"cuisine/cuisine-of-california-latino-and-hispanic-influence":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/cuisine-of-california-latino-and-hispanic-influence","n":"Cali-Mex cuisine","c":"#94bd5c","crumb":[["The Americas","cuisines#the-americas"],["Mexican-American cuisine","cuisine/mexican-american-cuisine"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in United States of America","intro":[["The cuisine of California reflects the diverse culture of California and is influenced largely by Indigenous, European American, Hispanic American  (Mexican, Latin American, Spanish), East Asian and Oceanian influences (Japanese, Chinese, Korean, Filipino, Vietnamese), and Middle Eastern and Mediterranean influences, as well as the food trends and traditions of larger American cuisine."],["The main trends were influenced by a combination of Mediterranean climate, geography and geology of the region's proximity to the ocean, its movie roots in Hollywood, its technology roots in Silicon Valley and the Napa wine country, as well as its major produce production. California used to be part of Mexico, which influenced the state's food."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"cuisine-of-california-latino-and-hispanic-influence"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cuisine_of_California#Latino_and_Hispanic_influence"}],"sections":[{"h":"Dishes","count":4,"links":[["Celery Victor","dish/celery-victor"],["Green goddess dressing","dish/green-goddess-dressing"],["Hangtown fry","dish/hangtown-fry"],["Oysters Kirkpatrick","dish/oysters-kirkpatrick"]]},{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[["Mexican-American cuisine","cuisine/mexican-american-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cookbooks","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"Fast and Fresh Cal-Mex Cooking: West Coast-Inspired Dinners in 30 Minutes or Less","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Caitlin Prettyman","note":"Quick Cal-Mex weeknight dishes.","url":"https://openlibrary.org/isbn/9798890030306","suggested":true,"isbn":"9798890030306"}]},{"h":"Key ingredients","links":[["Bacon","ingredient/bacon"],["Oyster","ingredient/oyster"],["Bell peppers","ingredient/bell-peppers"],["Broth","ingredient/broth"],["Celery","ingredient/celery"],["Romaine lettuce","ingredient/romaine-lettuce"],["Anchovy","ingredient/anchovy"],["Black pepper","ingredient/black-pepper"],["Chervil","ingredient/chervil"],["Chives","ingredient/chives"],["Lemon","ingredient/lemon"],["Mayonnaise","ingredient/mayonnaise"],["Sour cream","ingredient/sour-cream"],["Tarragon","ingredient/tarragon"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Cheese","ingredient/cheese"],["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"],["Scallion","ingredient/scallion"]],"note":"Most used across its dishes."},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Mexican-American cuisine","cuisine/mexican-american-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Within Cali-Mex cooking","count":1,"links":[["Korean-Mexican fusion","cuisine/korean-mexican-fusion"]]}],"cont":"Cuisine of the Americas","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/f/fd/Flickr_dongkwan_540812245--Shrimp_Tostada.jpg/500px-Flickr_dongkwan_540812245--Shrimp_Tostada.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Ernesto Andrade from San Francisco, California, USA","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flickr_dongkwan_540812245--Shrimp_Tostada.jpg"}},"cuisine/kyrgyz-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/kyrgyz-cuisine","n":"Kyrgyz cuisine","c":"#f0b340","crumb":[["Asia","cuisines#asia"],["Cuisine"]],"sub":"National cuisine of Kyrgyzstan","intro":[["Kyrgyz cuisine is the cuisine of the Kyrgyz, who comprise a majority of the population of Kyrgyzstan. The cuisine is similar in many aspects to that of their neighbors."],["Traditional Kyrgyz food revolves around mutton, beef and horse meat, as well as various dairy products. The preparation techniques and major ingredients have been strongly influenced by the nation's historically nomadic way of life. Thus, many cooking techniques are conducive to the long-term preservation of food. Mutton and beef are the favorite meats, although in modern times many Kyrgyz are unable to afford them regularly."],["Kyrgyzstan is home to many nationalities and their various cuisines. In larger cities, such as Bishkek, Osh, Jalal-Abad, and Karakol, various national and international cuisines can be found. Non-Kyrgyz cuisines that are particularly common and popular in Kyrgyzstan include Uyghur, Dungan, Uzbek, and Turkish cuisines, representing the largest minorities in the country."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"kyrgyz-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kyrgyz_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Dishes","count":11,"links":[["Beshbarmak","dish/beshbarmak"],["Boortsog","dish/boortsog"],["Chorba","dish/chorba"],["Dimlama","dish/dimlama"],["Kuurdak","dish/kuurdak"],["Naryn (dish)","dish/naryn-dish"],["Orama (dish)","dish/orama-dish"],["Pilaf","dish/pilaf"],["Qatlama","dish/qatlama"],["Qazı","dish/qaz"],["Shakarap","dish/shakarap"]]},{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[]},{"h":"Cookbooks","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"Red Sands: Reportage and Recipes Through Central Asia, from Hinterland to Heartland","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Caroline Eden, 2020","note":"Travel writing and recipes across the five Central Asian republics, not this cuisine alone.","url":"","suggested":true}]},{"h":"Key ingredients","links":[["Onion","ingredient/onion"],["Noodles","ingredient/noodles"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Beef","ingredient/beef"],["Carrot","ingredient/carrot"],["Lamb","ingredient/lamb"],["Potato","ingredient/potato"],["Butter","ingredient/butter"],["Cream","ingredient/cream"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Milk","ingredient/milk"],["Yeast","ingredient/yeast"],["Beans","ingredient/beans"],["Legumes","ingredient/legumes"],["Vegetables","ingredient/vegetables"],["Brassica oleracea","ingredient/brassica-oleracea"],["Veal","ingredient/veal"],["Noodle","ingredient/noodle"],["Animal fat","ingredient/animal-fat"],["Brassica","ingredient/brassica"],["Cucurbita","ingredient/cucurbita"],["Pumpkin","ingredient/pumpkin"],["Animal fats and oils","ingredient/animal-fats-and-oils"],["Broth","ingredient/broth"]],"note":"Most used across its dishes."}],"cont":"Asian cuisine","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/1/18/%D0%91%D0%B5%D1%88%D0%B1%D0%B0%D1%80%D0%BC%D0%B0%D0%BA1.jpg/500px-%D0%91%D0%B5%D1%88%D0%B1%D0%B0%D1%80%D0%BC%D0%B0%D0%BA1.jpg","w":500,"h":667,"by":"Sakateka","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%91%D0%B5%D1%88%D0%B1%D0%B0%D1%80%D0%BC%D0%B0%D0%BA1.jpg"}},"cuisine/taiwan-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/taiwan-cuisine","n":"Taiwan cuisine","c":"#f0b340","crumb":[["Asia","cuisines#asia"],["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine"]],"sub":"National cuisine of Taiwan","intro":[["Taiwanese cuisine is a popular style of food with several variations, including Chinese and that of Taiwanese indigenous peoples, with the earliest cuisines known of being the indigenous ones. With over a hundred years of historical development, southern Fujian cuisine has had the most profound impact on mainstream Taiwanese cuisine but it has also been influenced by Hakka cuisine, the cuisines of the waishengren (people of other provinces), and Japanese cuisine."],["Taiwan's cuisine is tied to its history of colonization and modern politics makes the description of Taiwanese cuisine difficult. As Taiwan developed economically, fine dining became increasingly popular. Taiwanese cuisine has significant regional variations."],["Night markets in Taiwan form a significant part of the food culture. Vegetarian and vegan food are very common. Taiwanese cuisine is popular around the world with some items like bubble tea and Taiwanese fried chicken becoming global phenomena."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"taiwan-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taiwan_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Dishes","count":29,"links":[["Ageh (food)","dish/ageh-food"],["Alivongvong","dish/alivongvong"],["Apple bread","dish/apple-bread"],["Bah-uân","dish/bah-uan"],["Braised pork rice","dish/braised-pork-rice"],["Coffin bread","dish/coffin-bread"],["Doujiang","dish/doujiang"],["Egg yolk pastry","dish/egg-yolk-pastry"],["Iron egg","dish/iron-egg"],["Kiâm-piánn","dish/kiam-piann"],["Ló͘-bah-pn̄g","dish/lo-bah-png"],["Mongolian barbecue","dish/mongolian-barbecue"],["Peanut ice cream roll","dish/peanut-ice-cream-roll"],["Penglai rice","dish/penglai-rice"],["Pineapple cake","dish/pineapple-cake"],["Pineapple shrimp balls","dish/pineapple-shrimp-balls"],["Pork ball","dish/pork-ball"],["Rechao","dish/rechao"],["Shuangbaotai","dish/shuangbaotai"],["Small sausage in large sausage","dish/small-sausage-in-large-sausage"],["Taiwanese beef noodle soup","dish/taiwanese-beef-noodle-soup"],["Taiwanese fried chicken","dish/taiwanese-fried-chicken"],["Taiwanese fried chicken cutlet","dish/taiwanese-fried-chicken-cutlet"],["Tàⁿ-á-mī","dish/ta-a-mi"],["Tea egg","dish/tea-egg"],["Ti-hueh-kué","dish/ti-hueh-kue"],["Tshik-á-mī","dish/tshik-a-mi"],["Tube rice pudding","dish/tube-rice-pudding"],["Xiaolongbao","dish/xiaolongbao"]]},{"h":"Recipe sites","count":2,"rows":[{"name":"Cooking in Chinglish","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"cookinginchinglish.com","note":"Taiwanese home recipes from Edwina, who grew up in Taiwan.","url":"https://cookinginchinglish.com","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Tiny Urban Kitchen: Taiwanese Recipes","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"tinyurbankitchen.com","note":"Small set of Taiwanese recipes from Jen Che, a Taiwanese American blogger in Hong Kong.","url":"https://tinyurbankitchen.com/taiwanese-recipes/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"Cookbooks","count":3,"rows":[{"name":"Made in Taiwan","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Clarissa Wei, 2023","note":"Taiwanese recipes and food culture from journalist Clarissa Wei.","url":"https://www.simonandschuster.com/books/Made-in-Taiwan/Clarissa-Wei/9781982198978","suggested":true,"isbn":"9781982198978"},{"name":"The Food of Taiwan: Recipes from the Beautiful Island","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Cathy Erway, 2015","note":"Survey of Taiwanese home and night-market cooking by a Taiwanese American food writer.","url":"https://openlibrary.org/isbn/9780544303010","suggested":true,"isbn":"9780544303010"},{"name":"First Generation","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Frankie Gaw, 2022","note":"Taiwanese American family recipes and stories from Frankie Gaw.","url":"https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/690431/first-generation-by-frankie-gaw/","suggested":true,"isbn":"9781984860767"}]},{"h":"Key ingredients","links":[["Pork","ingredient/pork"],["Rice","ingredient/rice"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Shiitake","in